{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s30-p01",
      "text": "Headphones are helpful.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p02",
      "text": "Many kids use them to listen to music or watch a cartoon.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p03",
      "text": "But headphones can be harmful too.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p04",
      "text": "They can cause hearing loss if the volume is too loud.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p05",
      "text": "Surveys show that one out of every ten kids in the US has some hearing loss.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p06",
      "text": "The cause is loud noise, like listening to a band at a noisy concert.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p07",
      "text": "Do you know how we hear?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p08",
      "text": "There are cells inside the ears that can't be seen with our eyes.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p09",
      "text": "We call them hair cells, said Jackie Clark, a scientist studying noises and ears.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p10",
      "text": "Sound can make the hair cells move back and forward.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p10.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p11",
      "text": "Think of the wind in the leaves or a waving flag.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p12",
      "text": "Once the cells are damaged by loud noises, they don't grow back.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p13",
      "text": "Sometimes there's tinnitus.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p14",
      "text": "It's like someone is playing a note on the flute for a long time.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p15",
      "text": "It shows we're losing hearing and in the worst case, becoming deaf.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p16",
      "text": "It makes us feel uneasy or even suffer an earache.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p17",
      "text": "It's necessary to protect our ears so that we don't end up in hospital.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p17.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p17.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p18",
      "text": "Let's follow some strict rules to protect our ears.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p18.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p18.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p19",
      "text": "Keep the volume low, and seldom use headphones for more than one hour at a time unless it's necessary.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p19.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p19.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p20-01",
      "text": "Don't use headphones in noisy places like a railway station,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p20-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p20-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p20-02",
      "text": "because you will need to turn up the volume to hear clearly.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p20-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p20-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p21",
      "text": "If I can hear what you're listening to when you're wearing your headphones, Ms Clark said, It's too loud.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p21.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p21.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30-p22",
      "text": "Although there are so many beautiful pieces of music, none should be listened to too loudly.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p22.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s30-p22.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
